classDiagram
    class Task {
        +str description
        +time time
        +date due_date
        +str frequency
        +bool is_completed
        +int duration_minutes
        +Priority priority
        +__post_init__()
        +mark_complete()
        +mark_incomplete()
        +create_next_occurrence(completed_on: date) Optional~Task~
    }

    class Pet {
        +str name
        +str species
        +int age
        +str notes
        +Task[] tasks
        +__post_init__()
        +add_task(task)
    }

    class Owner {
        +str name
        +Pet[] pets
        +__post_init__()
        +add_pet(pet)
        +get_all_tasks() Task[]
    }

    class Scheduler {
        +get_all_tasks(owner) Task[]
        +get_pending_tasks(owner) Task[]
        +filter_tasks(owner, is_completed: Optional~bool~, pet_name: Optional~str~) Task[]
        +sort_by_time(tasks) Task[]
        +organize_tasks(owner) Task[]
        +find_conflicts(owner) TaskConflict[]
        +get_conflict_warnings(owner) str[]
        +add_task(owner, pet, task) None
        +mark_task_complete(owner, task, completed_on: Optional~date~) None
    }

    class TaskConflict {
        +Pet first_pet
        +Task first_task
        +Pet second_pet
        +Task second_task
    }

    class Priority {
        <<enumeration>>
        LOW
        MEDIUM
        HIGH
    }

    Owner "1" o-- "0..*" Pet : manages
    Pet "1" *-- "0..*" Task : has
    Task --> Priority : has priority
    TaskConflict "1" --> "2" Pet : identifies pets in conflict
    TaskConflict "1" --> "2" Task : identifies overlapping tasks
    Scheduler ..> Owner : retrieves tasks through get_all_tasks()
    Scheduler ..> Pet : filters by name; finds task owner; adds next occurrence
    Scheduler ..> Task : filters, sorts, completes, creates recurrence
    Scheduler ..> TaskConflict : find_conflicts() returns records

    note for Scheduler "organize_tasks(): pending tasks by time, then priority; untimed tasks last. sort_by_time(): chronological, untimed tasks last. filter_tasks(): optional completion-status and pet-name filters. find_conflicts(): overlapping task intervals on the same due date. get_conflict_warnings(): converts conflict records to warning strings. mark_task_complete(): completes the task and adds its daily or weekly next occurrence to its pet."
